Package: mica-openssh
Version: 10.0p1-mica1
Source-Date-Epoch: 1792823171
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Mica OS <hi@micaos.dev>
Section: net
Priority: optional
Depends: mica-system, libaudit1, libcom-err2, libcrypt1, libgssapi-krb5-2, libkrb5-3, libpam0g, libselinux1, libssl3t64, libwrap0, libwtmpdb0, zlib1g
Provides: mica-ssh-server
Conflicts: mica-ssh
Description: Mica OS SSH: OpenSSH, disabled until micad enables it
 SSH as an option on the floor, in place of mica-ssh's dropbear: sshd,
 sshd-session, sshd-auth and ssh-keygen of the pinned openssh-server and
 openssh-client, carried as payload with their libraries in Depends (the Debian
 packages themselves need debconf, ucf and systemd's sysusers), and
 mica-sshd.service, its prestart /usr/lib/mica/mica-sshd-prestart and the preset
 that keeps the unit disabled. micad enables and starts it at runtime scope after
 writing /run/mica/sshd.env; the prestart makes the ed25519 host key on the
 STATE partition at the first start and renders /run/mica/sshd_config. The unit
 requires mica-shadow-reconcile.service, so the shadow file is built in RAM
 before a login can read it. No ssh client; SFTP is the root's
 /usr/lib/sftp-server.
 .
 UsePAM no: sshd checks a password through crypt(3) against /etc/shadow, as
 dropbear does, and refuses every login, keys included, to an account whose
 shadow field is `!`; `*` is an account with no password. The postinst adds
 sshd's privilege separation account, sshd, uid 22.
 .
 On an OpenRC root the same service is /etc/init.d/mica-sshd, in no runlevel:
 micad starts it the same way.
